# CODEOWNERS — Task #16 (Supply chain, CI/CD & responsible disclosure).
#
# Required reviewers for security-sensitive paths. Branch-protection should be
# configured to enforce CODEOWNERS review on all PRs that touch these areas.
# See docs/security/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md for the settings-as-code reference.
#
# Format:  <pattern>  <owner1> <owner2> ...
# Owners must be teams, not individuals, so coverage survives staff churn.
#
# All listed paths have been verified to exist in the tree as of 2026-04-19.
# Drift between this file and the real tree is a SEC-058 finding.

# Default fallback — every PR gets at least one core review.
*                                       @Manifest-Startup/core

# CI/CD pipeline + supply-chain configuration.
/.github/                               @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/platform
/.github/workflows/                     @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/platform
/.github/dependabot.yml                 @Manifest-Startup/security
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @Manifest-Startup/security

# Pre-commit, secret scanning, signing config.
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                @Manifest-Startup/security
/.gitleaks.toml                         @Manifest-Startup/security

# Container + runtime hardening.
/backend/dockerfile                     @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/platform
/docker-compose.yml                     @Manifest-Startup/platform
/build.sh                               @Manifest-Startup/platform
/scripts/                               @Manifest-Startup/platform

# Lockfiles — gates supply-chain risk; security must review every bump.
/backend/requirements.txt               @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/backend
/frontend/package.json                  @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/frontend
/frontend/package-lock.json             @Manifest-Startup/security @Manifest-Startup/frontend

